H7800.definition:
the same as H7799 (שׁוּשַׁן);
Shushan, a place in Persia
KJV: Shushan.

H7801.definition:
(Aramaic) of foreign origin;
a Shushankite (collectively) or inhabitants of some unknown place in Assyrian
KJV: Susanchites.

H7802.definition:
or (plural of former) שׁוֹשַׁנִּים עֵדוּתlemma שׁוֹשַׁנִּיס עֵדוּת samekh, corrected to שׁוֹשַׁנִּים עֵדוּת; from H7799 (שׁוּשַׁן) and H5715 (עֵדוּת); lily (or trumpet) of assemblage;
Shushan-Eduth or Shoshannim-Eduth, the title of a popular song
KJV: Shoshannim-Eduth, Shushan-eduth.

H7803.definition:
probably from H7582 (שָׁאָה) and the same as H8520 (תֶּלַח); crash of breakage;
Shuthelach, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Shuthelah.

H7804.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5800 (עָזַב);
to leave, i.e. (causatively) free
KJV: deliver.

H7805.definition:
a primitive root;
to tan (by sunburning); figuratively (as if by a piercing ray) to scan
KJV: look up, see.

H7806.definition:
a primitive root;
to twist (a thread of straw)
KJV: twine.

H7807.definition:
from H7817 (שָׁחַח);
sunk, i.e. downcast
KJV: [phrase] humble.

H7808.definition:
for H7879 (שִׂיחַ);
communion, i.e. (reflexively) meditation
KJV: thought.

H7809.definition:
a primitive root;
to donate, i.e. bribe
KJV: hire, give a reward.

H7810.definition:
from H7809 (שָׁחַד);
a donation (venal or redemptive)
KJV: bribe(-ry), gift, present, reward.

H7811.definition:
a primitive root;
to swim; causatively, to inundate
KJV: (make to) swim.

H7812.definition:
a primitive root;
to depress, i.e. prostrate (especially reflexive, in homage to royalty or God)
KJV: bow (self) down, crouch, fall down (flat), humbly beseech, do (make) obeisance, do reverence, make to stoop, worship.

H7813.definition:
from H7811 (שָׂחָה);
a pond (for swimming)
KJV: to swim in.

H7814.definition:
or שְׂחֹק; from H7832 (שָׂחַק);
laughter (in merriment or defiance)
KJV: derision, laughter(-ed to scorn, -ing), mocked, sport.

H7815.definition:
from H7835 (שָׁחַר);
dinginess, i.e. perhaps soot
KJV: coal.

H7817.definition:
a primitive root;
to sink or depress (reflexive or causative)
KJV: bend, bow (down), bring (cast) down, couch, humble self, be (bring) low, stoop.

H7818.definition:
a primitive root;
to tread out, i.e. squeeze (grapes)
KJV: press.

H7819.definition:
a primitive root;
to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre)
KJV: kill, offer, shoot out, slay, slaughter.

H7820.definition:
a primitive root (identical with H7819 (שָׁחַט) through the idea of striking);
to hammer out
KJV: beat.

H7822.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to burn;
inflammation, i.e. an ulcer
KJV: boil, botch.

H7823.definition:
or סָחִישׁ; from an unused root apparently meaning to sprout;
aftergrowth
KJV: (that) which springeth of the same.

H7824.definition:
from the same as H7828 (שַׁחַף);
a board (as chipped thin)
KJV: cieled with.

H7825.definition:
from H7812 (שָׁחָה);
a pit-fall (literally or figuratively)
KJV: destruction, pit.

H7826.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to roar;
a lion (from his characteristic roar)
KJV: (fierce) lion.

H7827.definition:
apparently from the same as H7826 (שַׁחַל) through some obscure idea, perhaps that of peeling off by concussion of sound;
a scale or shell, i.e. the aromatic mussel.
KJV: onycha.

H7828.definition:
from an unused root meaning to peel, i.e. emaciate;
the gull (as thin)
KJV: cuckoo.

H7829.definition:
from the same as H7828 (שַׁחַף);
emaciation
KJV: consumption.

H7830.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to strut;
haughtiness (as evinced by the attitude)
KJV: [idiom] lion, pride.

H7831.definition:
from the same as H7830 (שַׁחַץ); proudly;
Shachatsom, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shahazimah (from the margin).

H7832.definition:
a primitive root;
to laugh (in pleasure or detraction); by implication, to play
KJV: deride, have in derision, laugh, make merry, mock(-er), play, rejoice, (laugh to) scorn, be in (make) sport.

H7833.definition:
a primitive root;
to comminate (by trituration or attrition)
KJV: beat, wear.

H7834.definition:
from H7833 (שָׁחַק);
a powder (as beaten small); by analogy, a thin vapor; by extension, the firmament
KJV: cloud, small dust, heaven, sky.

H7835.definition:
a primitive root (identical with H7836 (שָׁחַר) through the idea of the duskiness of early dawn);
to be dim or dark (in color)
KJV: be black.

H7836.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to dawn, i.e. (figuratively) be (up) early at any task (with the implication of earnestness); by extension, to search for (with painstaking)
KJV: (do something) betimes, enquire early, rise (seek) betimes, seek diligently) early, in the morning).

H7837.definition:
from H7836 (שָׁחַר);
dawn (literal, figurative or adverbial)
KJV: day(-spring), early, light, morning, whence riseth.

H7838.definition:
or שָׁחוֹר; from H7835 (שָׁחַר);
properly, dusky, but also (absol.) jetty
KJV: black.

H7839.definition:
from H7836 (שָׁחַר);
a dawning, i.e. (figuratively) juvenescence
KJV: youth.

H7841.definition:
from H7836 (שָׁחַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has sought;
Shecharjah, an Israelite
KJV: Shehariah.

H7842.definition:
dual of H7837 (שַׁחַר); double dawn;
Shacharajim, an Israelite
KJV: Shaharaim.

H7843.definition:
a primitive root;
to decay, i.e. (causatively) ruin (literally or figuratively)
KJV: batter, cast off, corrupt(-er, thing), destroy(-er, -uction), lose, mar, perish, spill, spoiler, [idiom] utterly, waste(-r).

H7844.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7843 (שָׁחַת)
{to decay, i.e. (causatively) ruin (literally or figuratively)}
KJV: corrupt, fault.

H7845.definition:
from H7743 (שׁוּחַ);
a pit (especially as a trap); figuratively, destruction
KJV: corruption, destruction, ditch, grave, pit.

H7846.definition:
or סֵט; from H7750 (שׂוּט);
a departure from right, i.e. sin
KJV: revolter, that turn aside.

H7847.definition:
a primitive root;
to deviate from duty
KJV: decline, go aside, turn.

H7848.definition:
feminine of a derivative (only in the plural שִׁטִּים; meaning the sticks of wood) from the same as H7850 (שֹׁטֵט);
the acacia (from its scourging thorns)
KJV: shittah, shittim. See also H1029 (בֵּית הַשִּׁטָּה).

H7849.definition:
a primitive root;
to expand
KJV: all abroad, enlarge, spread, stretch out.

H7851.definition:
the same as the plural of H7848 (שִׁטָּה); acacia trees;
Shittim, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Shittim.

H7852.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to lurk for, i.e. persecute
KJV: hate, oppose self against.

H7853.definition:
a primitive root;
to attack, (figuratively) accuse
KJV: (be an) adversary, resist.

H7854.definition:
from H7853 (שָׂטַן);
an opponent; especially (with the article prefixed) Satan, the arch-enemy of good
KJV: adversary, Satan, withstand.

H7855.definition:
from H7853 (שָׂטַן);
opposition (by letter)
KJV: accusation.

H7856.definition:
the same as H7855 (שִׂטְנָה);
Sitnah, the name of a well in Pal
KJV: Sitnah.

H7857.definition:
a primitive root;
to gush; by implication, to inundate, cleanse; by analogy, to gallop, conquer
KJV: drown, (over-) flow(-whelm, rinse, run, rush, (throughly) wash (away).

H7858.definition:
or שֵׁטֶף; from H7857 (שָׁטַף);
a deluge (literally or figuratively)
KJV: flood, outrageous, overflowing.

H7859.definition:
(Aramaic) of uncertain derivation;
a side
KJV: side.

H7860.definition:
active participle of an otherwise unused root probably meaning to write;
properly, a scribe, i.e. (by analogy or implication) an official superintendent or magistrate
KJV: officer, overseer, ruler.

H7861.definition:
from the same as H7860 (שֹׁטֵר); magisterial;
Shitrai, an Israelite
KJV: Shitrai.

H7862.definition:
probably from H7737 (שָׁוָה);
a gift (as available)
KJV: present.

H7863.definition:
from the same as H7721 (שׂוֹא) by permutation;
elevation
KJV: excellency.

H7864.definition:
for H7724 (שְׁוָא);
Sheja, an Israelite
KJV: Sheva (from the margin).

H7865.definition:
from H7863 (שִׂיא); peak;
Sion, the summit of Mount Hermon
KJV: Sion.

H7866.definition:
from the same as H7722 (שׁוֹא); ruin;
Shijon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shihon.

H7867.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to become aged, i.e. (by implication) to grow gray
KJV: (be) grayheaded.

H7868.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7867 (שִׂיב)
{properly, to become aged, i.e. (by implication) to grow gray}
KJV: elder.

H7869.definition:
from H7867 (שִׂיב);
old age
KJV: age.

H7870.definition:
by permutation from H7725 (שׁוּב);
a return (of property)
KJV: captivity.

H7872.definition:
feminine of H7869 (שֵׂיב);
old age
KJV: (be) gray (grey hoar,-y) hairs (head,-ed), old age.

H7873.definition:
from H7734 (שׂוּג);
a withdrawal (into a private place)
KJV: pursuing.

H7874.definition:
a primitive root probably meaning to boil up (compare H7736 (שׁוּד)); used only as denominative from H7875 (שִׂיד);
to plaster
KJV: plaister.

H7875.definition:
from H7874 (שִׂיד)lemma שׂיד missing vowel, corrected to שִׂיד;
lime (as boiling when slacked)
KJV: lime, plaister.

H7876.definition:
a primitive root;
to keep in memory
KJV: be unmindful. (Render Deuteronomy 32:18, 'A Rock bore thee, thou must recollect; and (yet) thou hast forgotten,' etc.)

H7877.definition:
of unknown derivation;
Shiza, an Israelite
KJV: Shiza.

H7878.definition:
a primitive root;
to ponder, i.e. (by implication) converse (with oneself, and hence, aloud) or (transitively) utter
KJV: commune, complain, declare, meditate, muse, pray, speak, talk (with).

H7879.definition:
from H7878 (שִׂיחַ);
a contemplation; by implication, an utterance
KJV: babbling, communication, complaint, meditation, prayer, talk.

H7880.definition:
from H7878 (שִׂיחַ);
a shoot (as if uttered or put forth), i.e. (generally) shrubbery
KJV: bush, plant, shrub.

H7881.definition:
feminine of H7879 (שִׂיחַ);
reflection; be extension, devotion
KJV: meditation, prayer.

H7882.definition:
for H7745 (שׁוּחָה);
a pit-fall
KJV: pit.

H7883.definition:
or שִׁחוֹר; or שִׁחֹר; probably from H7835 (שָׁחַר); dark, i.e. turbid;
Shichor, a stream of Egypt
KJV: Shihor, Sihor.

H7884.definition:
from the same as H7883 (שִׁיחוֹר) and H3835 (לָבַן); darkish whiteness;
Shichor-Libnath, a stream of Palestine
KJV: Shihor-libnath.

H7885.definition:
from H7751 (שׁוּט); also compare H7752 (שׁוֹט)
an oar; a scourge (figuratively)
KJV: oar, scourge.

H7886.definition:
from H7951 (שָׁלָה); tranquil;
Shiloh, an epithet of the Messiah
KJV: Shiloh.

H7887.definition:
or שִׁלֹה; or שִׁילוֹ; or שִׁלוֹ; from the same as H7886 (שִׁילֹה);
Shiloh, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shiloh.

H7888.definition:
or שִׁילֹנִי; or שִׁלֹנִי; from H7887 (שִׁילֹה);
a Shilonite or inhabitant of Shiloh
KJV: Shilonite.

H7889.definition:
apparently for H3452 (יְשִׁימוֹן); desert;
Shimon, an Israelite
KJV: Shimon.

H7890.definition:
from an unused root meaning to urinate;
urine
KJV: piss.

H7891.definition:
or (the original form) שׁוּר; (1 Samuel 18:6), a primitive root (rather identical with H7788 (שׁוּר) through the idea of strolling minstrelsy);
to sing
KJV: behold (by mistake for H7789 (שׁוּר)), sing(-er, -ing man, -ing woman).

H7892.definition:
or feminine שִׁירָה; from H7891 (שִׁיר);
a song; abstractly, singing
KJV: musical(-ick), [idiom] sing(-er, -ing), song.

H7894.definition:
from the same as H7893 (שַׁיִשׁ); whiteness;
Shisha, an Israelite
KJV: Shisha.

H7895.definition:
or שׁוּשַׁק; of Egyptian derivation;
Shishak, an Egyptian king
KJV: Shishak.

H7896.definition:
a primitive root;
to place (in a very wide application)
KJV: apply, appoint, array, bring, consider, lay (up), let alone, [idiom] look, make, mark, put (on), [phrase] regard, set, shew, be stayed, [idiom] take.

H7897.definition:
from H7896 (שִׁית);
a dress (as put on)
KJV: attire.

H7898.definition:
from H7896 (שִׁית);
scrub or trash, i.e. wild growth of weeds or briers (as if put on the field)
KJV: thorns.

H7899.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ) in the sense of H7753 (שׂוּךְ);
a brier (as of a hedge)
KJV: prick.
